WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:51.250
Sexual comedy is one of the most universal
and popular genres of comedy in cinema.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.920
It's something pretty much every adult can relate
to and has the potential for big laughs. While

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.140
often used for comedic effect, I want to look
at how sexual imagery, specifically phallic

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.490
symbols, can be used to achieve dramatic effects.
Filmmakers can use phallic symbols to tremendously

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.149
contribute to the visual storytelling of a
film.

00:01:14.149 --> 00:01:17.989
Penis shapes are everywhere, and while not always acknowledged, there’s no doubt that skyscrapers

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:25.920
guns

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.140
or even a pipe

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.399
can be treated as phallic symbols. Psychologist Sigmund

00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:49.749
Freud is famous for theorizing that we notice
these objects are phallic on a subconscious

00:01:49.749 --> 00:01:54.119
level. In a similar way of thinking, filmmakers
use phallic symbols in place of actual sex

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:57.280
to get a subconscious emotional reaction from
the viewer.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.770
The simplest and most noticeable use of a
phallic symbol is to imply sex. In film, sex

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:05.479
is more often implied than actually shown,
especially with strict censorship during the

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:09.819
Golden Age of Cinema that banned showing sex
on screen, so instead of actual sex, we see

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:13.599
sex represented in a phallic object.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:26.400
The object can be anything, from a bedpost in The Birth of a Nation, a train entering a

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:33.180
tunnel in North by Northwest, a man pumping
gas into a woman’s car in Written on the

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:42.250
Wind, or a gun in Bonnie and Clyde. Through
a phallic symbol, we see there’s some kind

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.730
of sexual relationship or desired sexual relationship
between the two characters.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:51.030
Another common form of phallic symbol is to
show masculinity. A gun is a powerful phallic

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:54.870
symbol that indicates the masculinity of a
character. A big gun means you’re manly,

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.879
and the heroes in classic action movies seem
to always have ridiculously sized weapons.

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:01.079
And if a girl has a big gun, we know she’s reversing

00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:05.250
gender roles and taking on masculine qualities.
Small guns, on the other hand, are a sign

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.590
of weakness or vulnerability.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.800
The gun size issue even gets addressed in the James Bond

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:25.489
film Dr. No. As a spy, Bond has to conceal
a small gun, but the film makes it clear that

00:03:25.489 --> 00:03:33.180
it’s still manly. Another example is Written
on the Wind. When Kyle threatens Mitch with

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.900
a pistol, the small size of the gun further
reinforces the idea that Kyle is cowardly,

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:42.129
weak, and feminine. He doesn’t appear threatening
with such a small weapon. This parallels nicely

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:47.379
with the fact that Kyle is impotent and so
he’s missing a major aspect of being a man.

00:03:47.379 --> 00:03:51.569
Phallic symbols can also be used to convey
domination and control. We see this symbolism

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:56.560
hyperbolically in A Clockwork Orange. A Clockwork
Orange conveys the idea that if you can expose

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:01.040
someone sexually, you have complete and utter
domination over them. So when Alex wears a

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.989
phallic mask and beats the couple with a phallic
stick or uses a phallic statue to toy with

00:04:05.989 --> 00:04:10.290
an old lady, he’s asserting his complete
control over them. It shows that to physically

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:14.840
dominate someone is to also sexually dominate
someone. Sex and violence go hand in hand.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.000
Phallic symbols aid the visual storytelling
of the film because they help show Alex go

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.370
from dominating to being dominated. He goes
from overpowering everyone

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.510
to literally being squished by authority.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:33.600
Alien uses phallic symbols to convey fear.
The writer of the film intentionally made

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.479
Alien contain rape imagery to make the film
more terrifying.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.960
The parallels between the alien
attacks and real-life rape make the alien

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.810
attacks more horrific. Getting raped is a
scary thing, and the writers use the horrors

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:17.139
of rape to make the alien a scarier villain.
The design of the alien is very phallic, and

00:05:17.139 --> 00:05:21.759
the set pieces look equally as phallic and
vaginal. This design was done very intentionally

00:05:21.759 --> 00:05:26.339
by set designer H.R. Giger.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:42.180
From the erect mouth inside alien, to the face-huger laying eggs orally,

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:45.240
to the phallic chest buster, the whole alien is phallic

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:54.240
but instead of using phallic symbols to show manliness or domination, Alien uses phallic symbols to

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.970
show us being sexually dominated by the alien.
The phallic symbols evoke terror by making

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:03.270
the humans sexual victims to the alien. The
phallic symbols add to visual storytelling

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:08.190
in the film by making the alien attacks visually
and emotionally similar to sexual assault.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:11.699
Phallic symbols work even when they’re subtle.
A film like The Social Network is a perfect

00:06:11.699 --> 00:06:15.789
opportunity to use phallic symbols because
the whole film revolves around the fight for

00:06:15.789 --> 00:06:19.919
power, sex, and high social status. The Winklevoss
twins take Mark Zuckerburg to their final

00:06:19.919 --> 00:06:23.830
club house as a way to show off their high
status and power in order to help convince

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:27.599
Mark to work for them. They offer him a sandwich
to further show off their luxuries, and the

00:06:27.599 --> 00:06:36.160
way it’s presented to him is just so…
oddly phallic. And then he holds it like this…

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:40.349
and then after Mark questions their idea and
internally thinks of a better one, he holds

00:06:40.349 --> 00:06:47.000
the sandwich like this. Is it just a coincidence?
Maybe. But maybe not.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:51.660
There’s definitely a point where the analysis
of phallic symbols becomes overkill. Sigmund

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:55.590
Freud once said, “Sometimes, a cigar is
just a cigar.” Not everything that looks

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:59.440
phallic has some sexual meaning. But when
used intentionally, a phallic symbol can be

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:03.599
a powerful visual that adds meaning to what’s
happening on screen. So the next time you

00:07:03.599 --> 00:07:07.349
watch a film with your friends and notice
a phallic symbol, feel free to point it out,

00:07:07.349 --> 00:07:09.909
just don’t be a huge dick about it.

00:07:41.699 --> 00:07:42.419
Thanks for watching.

